{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And she shall draw off his shoe.</b> Of leather, as it is written: ואנעלך תחש, and 'on the right foot' — we learn רגל רגל from the metzora." "<b>And she shall draw off his shoe.</b> According to its plain sense: to transfer to him the inheritance of his dead brother, as we find with Boaz, to fulfill every matter — 'a man drew off his shoe and gave it to his fellow.' And as a response to the sectarians: 'וחלצה נעלו' means — if you wish to say 'I will perform yibum for you,' I will treat you like a maidservant to my master, and he will reply to her: 'I did not wish to take her.'" "<b>And she shall spit before him.</b> In order to disgrace him, for having rejected her — to say: since you do not desire me, I care for you no more than for this spittle." "<b>And she shall answer and say.</b> In order to disgrace him and to settle her mind."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "The final quotation 'לא חפצתי לקחתה' alludes to Ruth 4:13 but the subject and addressee are somewhat ambiguous in the Hebrew; translated literally preserving the ambiguity."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:15.949614726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}